      \field{abstract}{The automatic analysis of images in the historical sciences often requires the identification of objects. Object identification is a well-researched problem for modern photographs; however, for historical material, annotations are often necessary. We present a solution for finding objects without manual work. The method consists of a style transfer of images from the {COCO} dataset into the domain using {CycleGAN} and training with items obtained through pseudo-labelling on the original and the additional transferred {COCO} images. Different strategies to assemble the dataset are compared. The best method obtains an F1 score of 0.58 for 15 object types without any labelling.}
